# Pearmo website — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development, or set these in
# Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables for deployments.
#
# All three are NEXT_PUBLIC_*, meaning they are inlined into the client bundle
# at build time and are visible to anyone who views source. That is correct for
# these values — verification tokens are published in a <meta> tag by design and
# carry no secret. Never add a real secret with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
#
# Changing any of these requires a redeploy: Next.js substitutes them at build
# time, not at runtime.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical origin
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Overrides the default in src/lib/site.ts (https://www.pearmo.com).
#
# Leave UNSET in production — the built-in default is already correct, and
# `isProductionSite` only evaluates true when the resolved URL matches that
# default exactly. Setting this to anything else switches the whole site to
# noindex + `Disallow: /`, which is the intended behaviour for previews but
# would silently deindex production.
#
# Only set this if the canonical host changes (e.g. the apex becomes primary).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.pearmo.com


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Search Console
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ONLY needed for a URL-prefix property. The recommended setup is a Domain
# property, which is verified by a DNS TXT record and needs no code and no
# env var — leave this unset in that case.
#
# If you do use a URL-prefix property: Search Console offers an "HTML tag"
# method that gives you
#     <meta name="google-site-verification" content="AbC123..." />
# Paste ONLY the content value here, not the whole tag.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bing Webmaster Tools
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed if you verify Bing by importing the property from Google Search
# Console, which is the fastest route and carries verification across.
#
# For manual meta-tag verification, Bing gives you
#     <meta name="msvalidate.01" content="A1B2C3..." />
# Paste ONLY the content value here.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BING_SITE_VERIFICATION=
